 > - This package doesn't modify the pose information it receives.
 > - It only modifies NDT covariance values under certain conditions.
 
+The backward-compatible `fusion_policy` parameter selects one of three behaviors:
+
+- `official` (default) preserves the upstream source-selection and NDT covariance
+  interpolation behavior described below.
+- `ndt_primary_covariance` always forwards every valid, fresh NDT observation
+  unchanged and additionally forwards a valid, fresh and threshold-qualified GNSS
+  observation. GNSS is never used without a fresh NDT observation and never changes
+  the NDT pose or covariance.
+- `ndt_primary_position` has the same NDT-primary topology, but treats GNSS as an
+  x/y position observation. It keeps the measured GNSS position and covariance,
+  carries the latest NDT orientation with a deliberately uninformative yaw variance,
+  and removes yaw cross-covariances. This avoids counting an INSPVAX/INS yaw as an
+  independent GNSS observation when the EKF already consumes the same inertial
+  source. The default remains `official`; this policy requires separate validation
+  before product use.
+
+`ndt_primary_position` also exposes two disabled-by-default consistency gates:
+`gnss_ndt_max_stamp_delta_sec` and `gnss_ndt_xy_innovation_max_m`. They are
+intended for separately controlled experiments; a non-zero value rejects a GNSS
+position that is not timestamp-close to, or is too far from, the latest NDT
+observation.
+
 ## Assumptions
 
 - The NDT matcher provides a pose with a fixed covariance.
